00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,720
So we talked about grains.

00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:57,240
So grains are the best way to help the body

00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:01,120
maintain and gain some weight.

00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,760
So certainly organic grains are best

00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:07,960
and then gluten-free grains are preferred.

00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,360
You might be on a gluten-free diet as well

00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,480
or limited gluten diet.

00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,640
And so just gluten can be inflammatory

00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,200
and so we want to be mindful of that.

00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:20,360
But definitely organic.

00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:25,480
So your grains are not laced with any herbicides, pesticides,

00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,280
things like that.

00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:30,440
So getting grains and so really with every meal

00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:33,040
you can get some grains in.

00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:38,040
The other thing too is calorie-dense foods, so fats.

00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,480
So try to snack on different assortments of nuts

00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,720
and seeds throughout the day.

00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:48,840
You can put things that are high in fat into smoothies

00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,640
if you're doing a daily smoothie.

00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:54,160
So you could put avocados into a smoothie.

00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:56,000
You can put sweet potato into a smoothie.

00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,600
You can put coconut oil into a smoothie.

00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,840
So just trying to get some calorie-dense foods

00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,680
in as often as possible.

00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:10,880
You can top foods with things like olive oil.

00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,680
So if you're making some roasted vegetables,

00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:19,440
just load on some olive oil over the top and consume that.

00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:25,800
And just trying to keep those calories in snacking

00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:29,920
throughout the day, we do have a little list

00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:32,880
that gives you some tips and some resources.

00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:37,160
So certainly if you would like that for healthy weight gain

00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,880
reach out to your liaison and we can email that to you.

00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:44,040
But ultimately it's trying to get calorie-dense foods

00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:48,760
in as often as possible to consume grains

00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:52,320
and to just use snacks.

00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:58,800
You can use some plant-based protein powder as well.

00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,400
OK, the next question.

00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,720
My husband has had four rounds of chemo.

00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,760
Is there anything he can do to combat the fatigue?

00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:08,960
So the biggest thing to help with side effects of chemo

00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,560
is to follow the chemo protocol.

00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,720
So I'm not sure if this person is actually following that or not.

00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:17,840
If people want the chemo protocol again,

00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:21,320
just email your liaison and we can send you

00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:22,920
the chemo protocol.

00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:26,920
The goal of the chemo protocol is to protect the healthy cells

00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:31,200
and to help the chemo target the cancerous cells.

00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,840
And so there's a number of different things you can do.

00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:38,480
And just quickly one of the things

00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:45,000
is to fast 24 hours prior to chemo, fasting,

00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,800
really cancerous cells become unstable.

00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,960
They're not as resilient when it comes to fasting.

00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:57,800
And the healthy cells are more resilient.

00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:02,520
And so continue to do just a 24 hour fast.

00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:06,320
And then things you can do within that 48 hour window

00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:11,120
of when you have chemotherapy 48 hours after.

00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,880
We don't want you to do any major detoxing.

00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,640
We don't want you to be doing some of the foot baths.

00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:20,480
We don't want you to be taking high antioxidant supplements.

00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:23,680
We don't want you to be doing coffee animals during this window

00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:27,000
because we want to maximize chemo's effect.

00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:32,400
And within that 48 hours is when it's going to do its work.

00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:35,200
So after that 48 hour mark, we really want to pull it out

00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,000
of the system as much as possible.

00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,080
So then we reintroduce those things that we had you hold off on

00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,160
for that 48 hours.

00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:47,160
So again, the antioxidants, the coffee animals can be resumed.

00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,560
The foot bath sessions can be resumed.

00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,800
So all of these things to really rapidly try to detox the body

00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,240
to get it out of the system where it's more likely

00:04:56,240 --> 00:05:01,440
to damage healthy cells after that 48 hour point.

00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:05,840
So following that chemo protocol can help with fatigue.

00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,320
You know, really when you're taking chemo,

00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,880
you're damaging all cells.

00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:12,520
And so part of what is being damaged is the ATP,

00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,280
or excuse me, the mitochondria of the cell.

00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,800
And the mitochondria are what produce ATP,

00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:21,040
which is what our cells use to perform their function.

00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:24,240
It's the fuel source they need to work.

00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,680
So when you're rapidly killing off cells,

00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:30,120
you're rapidly killing off for damaging mitochondria.

00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:33,480
And so that is likely why you're feeling that fatigue.

00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,040
So follow the chemo protocol.

00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,720
That's the best way to protect yourselves

00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:42,120
from some of the side effects of chemo.

00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:46,000
All right, I tried to run some of the other programs on my rife,

00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,760
but I got a message about a USB and something

00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,880
about a generator not being connected.

00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,680
What am I doing wrong?

00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:59,160
So it is common to have some miscommunication

00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,400
between the rife machine and the computer.

00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,960
So first, you want to make sure that the USB cord

00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,240
is actually connected.

00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,920
Sometimes it can come loose if it's bumped

00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:12,680
and it can kind of come out of the port.

00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,280
So make sure everything is connected.

00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,040
Usually if something is not connected,

00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:22,080
and then it suddenly recognizes as being connected,

00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:25,640
you'll hear kind of a little chime on the computer indicating,

00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:29,200
oh, we've now recognized a new connection.

00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:33,800
So you should hear that chime if something goes from disconnected

00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,160
to now connected.

00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,480
So listen for that.

00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,080
And the other thing that you can do

00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,680
is just power everything down.

00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:44,520
So turn off the rife machine and power it on the computer.

00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:47,520
And you need to do a complete shutdown of the computer

00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:50,880
not just closing it and putting it into sleep mode.

00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,960
So you have to find the power button, usually

00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:55,280
on the upper right or upper left corner

00:06:55,280 --> 00:07:01,600
of the bottom keyboard platform, sometimes depending

00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,160
on which laptop you had the power button

00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:07,880
might be along one of the sides, the edges of the computer.

00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:12,800
So locate the power button, hold it down for at least 10 seconds.

00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:17,760
And that is going to shut everything down in the computer,

00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:21,360
let it sit then for about 15 seconds.

00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,920
And then you can just tap the power button again

00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,320
to boot it back up.

00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,680
And it should cycle through the whole process

00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:31,600
of getting starting up again.

00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,880
You should see that sign in button to click

00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,480
to kind of get to your desktop.

00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:39,400
And then you're going to have to click on the true rife icon

00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:43,560
again to get to your software.

00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,920
So once you got the computer up and going again,

00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,400
then you can power on the rife machine.

00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:53,160
And again, listen for that little chime indicating,

00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:56,680
OK, we've now recognized that there is a new connection.

00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:01,160
And then everything should be running and working as usual.

00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,920
And it is good practice to just do that whole process

00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:07,600
that I just described, maybe one time a week,

00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:13,040
just to kind of reset everything, reestablish any missed communications.

00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:16,320
And so I would maybe just take a day of the week

00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,080
where you're just going to power everything down

00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,360
and then reboot it back up.

00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:22,160
But that does happen where you get that message

00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:24,720
that you're talking about once in a while.

00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,320
It just happened to me last night.

00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,840
I went to turn on the rife machine.

00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,920
You know, we ran it the night before.

00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:33,320
And I went to turn it on last night.

00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:38,200
And it was telling me that the generator was null

00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,920
or not connected, couldn't sense it.

00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:45,400
And so I had to do that same process, just reboot everything

00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,080
and that it worked fine.

00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:51,720
So that is the troubleshooting for that.

00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:57,480
